    <DataNode elementId="AT1G02730-MONOMER" textLabel="non-crystalline β-glucan synthase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SRW9" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="695" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The precise function of the CSLD5 (cellulose-synthase-like D5) enzyme has not yet been determined &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt;. Though csld5 mutants have reduced levels of xylan and homogalacturonan synthase activity and also show alterations in xylan occurrence, it seems unlikely that csld5 plays a direct role in forming these compounds |CITS: [17892446]|. In addition, although its protein sequence suggests that it should behave like a cellulose synthase, its Golgi apparatus location argues against its participation in crystalline cellulose synthesis at the plasma membrane |CITS: [17892446]|. The protein may still function as a &amp;beta;-glucan synthase but the exact linkage produced and compound formed remain unknown |CITS: [17892446]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G02730-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G02730.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9SRW9" />
